# Findings

## High — The runnable harness still contradicts the revised palette requirements

The prose was corrected, but `select_palette` remains unchanged: it filters for a single ANSI line containing both `group` and `title`, parses ANSI state with `boldAt`, and fails unless exactly one bold row is found. Every OpenCode music invocation still calls this helper, so the actual Phase 1 verify command continues to impose both forbidden gates before the authoritative media/UI proof can run.

The helper also captures `UI_TEXT` but emits only `UI_ANSI`, and logs `selected=<group>/<title>` rather than the literal submitted `query`. Thus the runnable evidence does not satisfy the revised acceptance check requiring the exact query and complete resulting text/ANSI palette.

Remove the same-line/bold parser from the music path and explicitly emit the query, `UI_TEXT`, and `UI_ANSI`. Keep the existing post-Enter canonical transition and required host UI convergence as execution proof.
